      "event_id": "run-35010564817-review-lifecycle",
      "findings": [
        {
          "evidence": "Candidate line 96 newly removes a null Int32 _id and returns removed=true. Insert(T) then calls _engine.Insert at line 20; Engine/Engine/Transaction.cs lines 89-92 commit and release the auto-transaction before control returns. Only afterward, Insert.cs line 27 invokes _id.Setter. Client/Mapper/Reflection/Reflection.Expression.cs lines 52-53 deliberately return a null setter for a get-only property, so this invocation throws NullReferenceException after commit. An executed net8.0 candidate repro using `public int? Id { get; }` produced `exception=System.NullReferenceException`, `immediate-count=1`, and `reopened-count=1`. At the base SHA the changed predicate leaves the null _id in place, so Engine/Engine/Insert.cs rejects id.IsNull inside AutoTransaction before storage and rolls back. The candidate therefore turns a failed call into a durable, caller-unacknowledged write. Validate writability before entering the engine or otherwise ensure ID copy-back cannot fail after commit.",
          "path": "LiteDB/Client/Database/Collections/Insert.cs",
          "severity": "major",
          "summary": "A get-only nullable integer ID throws after its insert has already committed"
        }
      ],
      "issue": 1002,
      "kind": "review",
      "outcome": "fail",
